<title>FRANCE: ADP export traffic down 1.8pct in Jan-Oct.</title>
<headline>ADP export traffic down 1.8pct in Jan-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air air cargo exports leeaving the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 484,155 tonnes in the first ten months of 1996, down 1.8 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP) afigures show.</p>
<p>Export traffic from the ADP, by region, in tonnes with percentage change on January-October 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p>  Domestic		 39,230     down  1.9pct</p>
<p>  European Union	 56,735     up    0.7</p>
<p>  Non-EU Europe	  10,646     down  4.5</p>
<p>  North Africa	    8,767     down 32.6</p>
<p>  Sub-Saharan Africa   39,307     up    0.9</p>
<p>  North America	 132,934     down  1.9</p>
<p>  French territories   22,180     down  3.6</p>
<p>  Latin America	  25,366     up    2.0</p>
<p>  Middle East	    48,412     up    7.2</p>
<p>  Far East		100,578     down  4.4</p>
<p>  Total		   484,155     down  1.8</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
